_exptl_absorpt_process_details
;
C. W. Dwiggins, Jr., Acta Cryst. A31, 395 (1975).
#;
#
#_exptl_absorpt_special_details
#;
Neutron linear absorption coefficient is wavelength dependent.
For each peak, the absorption coefficient mu is calculated as:
mu = 0.2650 + 0.0080/1.7982 * wavelength  [cm^-1^]
where
0.2650 cm^-1 is the absorption coefficient for total scattering;
0.0080 cm^-1 is the absorption coefficient for true absorption at 1.7982 A.

The value of 0.0269 (mm^-1^) shown in _exptl_absorpt_coefficient_mu
is the sample absorption coefficient for neutron wavelength at 1.0 \%A.
;
